v6.2 draft rule (to apply AFTER the v6.1 exam completes, tune-split justified):
replace the STEP 1 anchor-sign bullet with:
- The stated position direction contradicts what the record CLAIMS about its
  own result: the record presents a positive premium for the stated position
  while its anchor signs imply the opposite leg earned it. That hidden
  reversal is a defect. It is NOT a defect when the record openly reports
  that the stated position earned a negative or insignificant result -- an
  honestly disclosed loss is a finding (see Step 3), not a sign error.
